      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Besides deep breathing, there are several ways to stimulate the vagus nerve, including listening to soothing music, practicing yoga or tai chi, and engaging in activities that bring you joy or calmness, such as reading, meditation, or spending time with loved ones. Social activities, like conversation or even just smiling and laughing with others, can also stimulate the vagus nerve, as it triggers release of neurotransmitters like oxytocin, which is often referred to as the \"cuddle hormone\". Even laughing has been shown to have a direct impact on the vagus nerve.",
      "source": "target",
